From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nds-ports <nds-ports@localhost>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:39:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add Nintendo DS platform

Makefile.nds builds a DSi enhanced .nds with devkitARM and libnds/calico,
as Wolfenstein 3D v1.4 with the Apogee graphics layout, which also plays
the shareware and the GT/id/Activision data.

Wolf4SDL runs on an implementation of the parts of SDL 2 and SDL_mixer
it uses, in nds/, so its own code barely changes:

- Video: surfaces are 8-bit frames with the pitch of the 8bpp bitmap
  backgrounds they are copied into by DMA, page flipped on vblank. The
  affine background hardware scales 320x200 to 256x192 and a second,
  alpha blended layer half a pixel further smooths it. The palette of
  the screen surface is the hardware palette, so fades cost nothing.
- Input: START is the escape key, the other buttons are joystick 0 with
  the d-pad as its axes, and dragging the stylus turns like a mouse.
- Audio: chunks play on hardware channels 0-5, which do the resampling,
  volume and stereo panning, so the digitized sounds play as they are. A
  700 Hz thread runs the music hook and the post mix into a stream on
  channel 6, for the PC speaker.
- The OPL2 (opl_nds.c) replaces the MAME emulator, which took most of
  the ARM9: every OPL channel is a hardware channel looping one period
  of the waveform its two FM operators make, at its pitch, with the
  envelopes, key scaling and levels of the MAME emulator in software.

Startup (wl_nds.c) finds the game data in /data/wolf3d/ on the SD card,
next to the .nds, at the SD root or embedded in the ROM through NitroFS,
the full game first, keeps the config and savegames in /data/wolf3d/
and reads extra arguments from args.txt there. Errors are shown on the
touch screen.

Also: the screen is 320x200, the buttons have DS defaults, the ray
caster, the scaler and the fixed point math run from ITCM, and new
savegames are named after the episode and floor.
